      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Anomalous origin of the left anterior descending coronary artery from the right sinus of Valsalva has been described as a benign anomaly. Typically it takes one of two courses, intraseptal or prepulmonic (though pre-aortic and retro-aortic courses also have been described). We describe the treatment of a patient with prepulmonic route and a malignant course before revascularization."},
